# docs/WORKBUDDY-PLATFORM.md: "Files on the target machine have CRLF line
# endings. Preserve them or expect noisy diffs."
#
# Everything is stored LF in git and normalised on commit. The plugin payload —
# the directories copied into
#   C:/Users/<USER>/.workbuddy-ai/plugins/marketplaces/my-experts/plugins/
# — is checked out CRLF on every platform, so what is authored here is
# byte-identical to what sits on the Windows box and edits there produce clean
# diffs rather than whole-file rewrites.
#
# Applies from the next checkout. To convert an existing tree in place:
#   git add --renormalize .
#
# Scoped deliberately: tests/ and docs/ never leave this repo, so they stay
# native and this machine's diffs stay readable.

* text=auto

.codebuddy-plugin/** text eol=crlf
agents/** text eol=crlf
skills/** text eol=crlf
README.md text eol=crlf

avatars/** binary
*.png binary

# Reference snapshots are data, not payload prose. Checked out CRLF they would
# have different bytes on Windows than here, so any hash taken over the file
# would differ by platform — and a snapshot whose hash depends on where it was
# read is a snapshot that cannot prove it is unchanged. tools/fetch_references.py
# hashes parsed content rather than raw bytes for the same reason; this keeps
# the file itself byte-identical everywhere too.
skills/**/references/** -text
*.geojson -text
